<div class="pn-g300">

  {%- comment -%} ═══ HERO ═══ {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="hero-eyebrow">👀 The Book From the Video You Just Watched</p>
      <h1 class="hero-h1">Your Grandkid Asks 300 Questions a Week. Who's Answering Them?</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub"><strong>Right now, it's a screen.</strong> But it can be <strong>you</strong> instead.</p>
      <div class="hero-stars">
        <span class="stars-gold">★★★★★</span>
        <span><span class="stars-text">4.9</span> <span class="stars-sub">· 2,847 verified reviews</span></span>
        <span class="stars-text">Bestseller for Ages 6 to 12</span>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-cta-wrap" data-sticky-cta-bar>
        <a href="{{ section.settings.cta_url | default: 'https://primenaturals.store/products/kids-encyclopedia-100-000-whys' }}" class="cta-btn">GET 50% OFF ON THE BOOK →</a>
      </div>

      <p class="challenge-para">How many of these could <em>you</em> answer, off the top of your head, right now?</p>

      <div class="question-pills">
        <span class="q-pill">Why can water put out a fire?</span>
        <span class="q-pill">Why do flowers smell?</span>
        <span class="q-pill">Why does iron rust?</span>
        <span class="q-pill">Why shouldn't you touch a plug with wet hands?</span>
        <span class="q-pill">Why do we dream?</span>
        <span class="q-pill">Why is the sky blue?</span>
        <span class="q-pill">Why do some videos look blurry?</span>
        <span class="q-pill">Why can't we breathe underwater?</span>
        <span class="q-pill">Why do stars twinkle?</span>
        <span class="q-pill q-pill-dark">and hundreds more</span>
      </div>

      <p class="blurb-para">Your grandkid asks questions like these constantly. You don't need to know the answers — you need to know how to discover them together with this book.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ═══ BOOK SPREADS ═══ {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="book-spreads-wrap">
      <img class="book-spread-img" src="{{ 'spark-curiosity.png' | asset_url }}" alt="10,000 Why comic-style illustrated spread — science questions for kids" width="712" height="382" loading="eager">
      <img class="book-spread-img" src="{{ 'magnific_4second-loop-grandmothers.gif' | asset_url }}" alt="10,000 Why book spread with illustrated explanations" width="712" height="382" loading="eager">
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ═══ PULL QUOTE ═══ {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="pull-quote-card">
      <div class="pull-quote-avatar">
        <img src="{{ 'g300-avatar.png' | asset_url }}" alt="Grandparent narrator illustration" width="120" height="120" loading="lazy">
      </div>
      <div class="pull-quote-body">
        <p class="pull-quote-text">"When my grandkids asked me why the sky was blue, I realized I didn't actually know. So I found the book that did, and now <strong>they</strong> tell <strong>me</strong>. That's the whole point. Hundreds of questions, every answer drawn like a comic."</p>
        <p class="pull-quote-attr">— Why families are switching to 10,000 Why</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="answered-caption">Every one of those questions is answered like this.</p>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} ═══ NOT A TEXTBOOK ═══ {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="textbook-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="textbook-h2">Not a Textbook. A Comic They Can't Put Down.</h2>

      <div class="question-item">
        <p class="question-label">🔥 Physics · page 42</p>
        <h3 class="question-h3">Why Can Water Put Out a Fire?</h3>
        <p class="question-p">A grinning cartoon firefighter, a panicking flame, and an answer they'll repeat at dinner for a week. There's even a "You know what?" box with a fact most adults get wrong. We'll let them tell you that one.</p>
        <div class="question-highlight">Every page ends with a "You know what?" box, the fact that makes them say it out loud.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="question-item">
        <p class="question-label">⚡ Everyday Safety · page 57</p>
        <h3 class="question-h3">Why Shouldn't You Touch a Plug With Wet Hands?</h3>
        <p class="question-p">This one has a cartoon pig getting the shock of its life, and a real, kid-level explanation of why it happens. Much better learned from a funny drawing than the hard way.</p>
        <div class="question-highlight">Real safety, real science, delivered so it actually sticks.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="question-item">
        <p class="question-label">🌸 Biology · early chapters</p>
        <h3 class="question-h3">Why Do Flowers Have a Fragrance?</h3>
        <p class="question-p">Turns out a flower's smell is basically an advertisement aimed at bees. One question, and suddenly they understand pollination, seeds, and fruit, without ever feeling like a lesson.</p>
        <div class="question-highlight">One question quietly teaches five things. And there are hundreds more.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ═══ SOCIAL PROOF IMAGE ═══ {%- endcomment -%}
